    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1107">

                <pb facs="1093" n="1081" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg1081"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94115 Exchange/69: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-11T18:00:00+01:00">January 11, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6:42 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>246. American Interests—Japan. Legation’s 8210, December 30.<anchor n="50"
                        xml:id="d1107-f1"/> Swiss Foreign [Office?] official informally advised
                    Legation receipt telegram from Swiss Minister, Tokyo,<anchor n="51"
                        xml:id="d1107-f2"/> reporting further conversation with official [in]
                    Japanese Foreign Office regarding possibility third exchange. Swiss Foreign
                    Office official while stating unable transmit contents telegram by note informed
                    Legation orally that Japanese official stated questions of third exchange and
                    transportation to Japan of Red Cross supplies now Vladivostok (Department’s
                    2908, November 24<anchor n="52" xml:id="d1107-f3"/>) should be held in abeyance
                    until Japanese receive satisfactory reply their protests against attacks on 17
                    hospital ships<anchor n="53" xml:id="d1107-f4"/> which apparently transmitted
                    through Spanish Embassy, Washington.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
